# Line-ending policy.
#
# Deepsand's source is developed on Windows but half of it executes inside a
# Linux container. CRLF there is not cosmetic: a shell script whose shebang is
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` fails with
#
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# and the container never starts. Forcing LF on checkout makes that impossible
# regardless of the developer's `core.autocrlf` setting.
#
# See runtime/README.md and docs/SECURITY.md.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Everything that is read or executed by Linux, plus all project sources.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.cjs           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.jsonc         text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.rs            text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.lock          text eol=lf
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.tsx           text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf

# Windows shell scripts and batch files genuinely want CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending translated.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.lib   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary
